01:08:43,536 --> 01:08:45,496
Buy you a cup of coffee?

1142
01:08:47,582 --> 01:08:49,291
Hell, yes.

1143
01:08:50,210 --> 01:08:54,671
- Do you have to get back to the office?
- Nothing that can't wait.

1144
01:09:07,393 --> 01:09:08,769
I....

1145
01:09:08,937 --> 01:09:11,688
I drop down to the news studios
every now and then...

1146
01:09:11,856 --> 01:09:15,275
...and ask Howard Beale about you,
and he says you're doing fine. Are you?

1147
01:09:15,443 --> 01:09:16,777
No.

1148
01:09:17,237 --> 01:09:20,948
- Are you keeping busy?
- Oh, in a fashion.

1149
01:09:21,115 --> 01:09:25,118
This is the, uh, third funeral
I've been to in two weeks.

1150
01:09:25,286 --> 01:09:30,207
I have two other friends
in the hospital whom I visit regularly...

1151
01:09:30,375 --> 01:09:33,502
...and, uh, been to a couple of christenings.

1152
01:09:33,670 --> 01:09:37,923
All my friends seem to be dying
or having grandchildren.

1153
01:09:38,591 --> 01:09:40,801
You should be a grandfather yourself
about now.

1154
01:09:40,969 --> 01:09:43,595
You have a pregnant daughter
in Seattle, don't you?

1155
01:09:43,763 --> 01:09:48,600
Any day now.
My wife's out there for the occasion.

1156
01:09:52,814 --> 01:09:56,775
I've thought many times of calling you.

1157
01:09:58,111 --> 01:10:00,112
I wish you had.

1158
01:10:03,449 --> 01:10:07,411
You know, I bumped into Sibyl
the Soothsayer in the elevator last week.

1159
01:10:07,579 --> 01:10:11,123
I said, "You know, Sibyl,
about four months ago you predicted...

1160
01:10:11,291 --> 01:10:14,918
...I would get involved
with a craggy, middle-aged man...

1161
01:10:15,086 --> 01:10:18,630
...and so far, all that's happened
has been one many-splendored night.

1162
01:10:18,798 --> 01:10:21,717
I don't call that 'getting involved."'

1163
01:10:22,343 --> 01:10:26,221
And she said, "Don't worry, you will."

1164
01:10:28,641 --> 01:10:32,477
It was a many-splendored night,
wasn't it, Max?

1165
01:10:34,230 --> 01:10:36,189
Yes, it was.

1166
01:10:38,484 --> 01:10:40,986
Are we going to get involved, Max?

1167
01:10:43,531 --> 01:10:44,907
Yes.

1168
01:10:45,617 --> 01:10:50,746
I need to become involved very much.
How about you?

1169
01:10:52,498 --> 01:10:55,167
I've reached for the phone to call you
a hundred times.

1170
01:10:55,335 --> 01:10:58,545
I was sure you hated me for my part
in taking your news show away.

1171
01:11:00,340 --> 01:11:03,342
I probably did. I don't know anymore.

1172
01:11:03,927 --> 01:11:08,680
All I know is,
I can't get you out of my mind.

1173
01:11:13,227 --> 01:11:15,395
Marty.
Marty, I know what NBC offered them...

1174
01:11:15,563 --> 01:11:18,023
...so I'm saying go to 3.5...

1175
01:11:18,191 --> 01:11:21,109
...and I want an option
for a third run on all of them.

1176
01:11:21,277 --> 01:11:25,155
Marty, I'm in a big hurry and you and Charlie
are supposed to be negotiating this...

1177
01:11:25,323 --> 01:11:27,950
...so goodbye, good luck,
I'll see you Monday.

1178
01:11:30,370 --> 01:11:32,955
MAN: Jimmy Caan's agent just called
and says absolutely nix.

1179
01:11:33,122 --> 01:11:35,540
DIANA: Can't win them all.
- Where can I reach you later?

1180
01:11:35,708 --> 01:11:37,542
DIANA:
You can't. I'll be gone all weekend.

1181
01:11:42,632 --> 01:11:44,883
NBC's offering $3.25 mil...

1182
01:11:45,051 --> 01:11:47,260
...per package
of five James Bond movies...

1183
01:11:47,428 --> 01:11:52,641
...and I think I'm gonna steal them
for $3.5 million with a third run.

1184
01:12:01,067 --> 01:12:03,485
DIANA: And I'm gonna stick
The Mao Tse-Tung Hour in at 8...

1185
01:12:03,653 --> 01:12:06,947
...because we're having a lot of trouble
selling The Mao Tse-Tung Hour.

1186
01:12:07,115 --> 01:12:08,699
This way....

1187
01:12:09,283 --> 01:12:12,285
[PIANO PLAYING SOFT MUSIC]

1188
01:12:16,749 --> 01:12:21,795
That Mao Tse-Tung Hour's
turning into one big pain in the ass.

1189
01:12:22,922 --> 01:12:27,175
We're having heavy legal problems
with the federal government right now.

1190
01:12:28,261 --> 01:12:31,054
Two FBI guys turned up
in Hackett's office last week...

1191
01:12:31,222 --> 01:12:33,724
...and served us with a subpoena.

1192
01:12:34,851 --> 01:12:39,438
They heard about our Flagstaff bank
rip-off film and they want it.

1193
01:12:40,523 --> 01:12:43,316
Hackett told the FBI to fuck off.

1194
01:12:47,280 --> 01:12:48,363
[DIANA LAUGHS]

1195
01:12:48,531 --> 01:12:50,365
DIANA:
No, but we're getting around the FBI...

1196
01:12:50,533 --> 01:12:54,036
...by doing the show in collaboration
with the news division.

1197
01:12:54,203 --> 01:12:57,080
We're standing on the First Amendment,
Freedom of the Press...

1198
01:12:57,248 --> 01:12:59,124
...and the right to protect our sources.

1199
01:12:59,292 --> 01:13:02,586
Walter thinks we can knock out
the misprision of felony charge. Ha, ha.

1200
01:13:08,801 --> 01:13:10,302
[DIANA LAUGHING]

1201
01:13:10,470 --> 01:13:13,555
But he says absolutely nix
on going to series.

1202
01:13:13,723 --> 01:13:18,685
They'll hit us with conspiracy
and inducement to commit a crime.

1203
01:13:18,853 --> 01:13:21,188
Christ, it's cold in here.

1204
01:13:21,355 --> 01:13:24,524
See, we're paying these nuts
from the Ecumenical Liberation Army...

1205
01:13:24,692 --> 01:13:27,778
...$10,000 a week in order to turn in
authentic film footage...

1206
01:13:27,945 --> 01:13:29,946
...of their revolutionary activities...

1207
01:13:30,114 --> 01:13:33,325
...and that can constitute inducement
to commit a crime.

1208
01:13:33,493 --> 01:13:37,788
And Walter says we'll all wind up
in federal prison.

1209
01:13:38,164 --> 01:13:41,208
I said,
"Walter, let the government sue us.

1210
01:13:41,375 --> 01:13:45,378
Let the federal government sue us.
We'll take them to the Supreme Court.

1211
01:13:45,546 --> 01:13:49,007
We'll be front page, mm, for months.

1212
01:13:49,258 --> 01:13:52,052
The New York Times
and The Washington Post...

1213
01:13:52,220 --> 01:13:55,180
...will be writing two editorials a week
about us.

1214
01:13:55,348 --> 01:13:58,600
We'll be front page for months.
We'll have more press than Watergate."

1215
01:13:58,768 --> 01:14:03,313
All I need is six weeks' federal litigation...

1216
01:14:03,481 --> 01:14:07,025
...and The Mao Tse-Tung Hour
can start carrying its own time slot.

1217
01:14:07,193 --> 01:14:08,652
[DIANA SHRIEKS]

1218
01:14:10,488 --> 01:14:12,864
[PANTING]

1219
01:14:17,036 --> 01:14:18,578
[DIANA SIGHS]

1220
01:14:23,626 --> 01:14:27,587
What's really bugging me now
is my daytime programming.

1221
01:14:28,589 --> 01:14:31,174
NBC's got a lock on daytime...

1222
01:14:31,342 --> 01:14:33,468
...with their lousy game shows...

1223
01:14:34,011 --> 01:14:36,388
...and I'd like to bust them.

1224
01:14:36,806 --> 01:14:40,058
I'm thinking of doing
a homosexual soap opera.

1225
01:14:40,226 --> 01:14:41,935
The Dykes.

1226
01:14:42,728 --> 01:14:46,231
The heart-rendering saga
about a woman hopelessly in love...

1227
01:14:46,399 --> 01:14:50,694
...with her husband's mistress.
What do you think?

1228
01:15:02,748 --> 01:15:04,207
How long has it been going on?

1229
01:15:06,669 --> 01:15:08,253
A month.

1230
01:15:10,256 --> 01:15:13,466
I thought it was a transient thing,
blow over in a week.

1231
01:15:14,886 --> 01:15:20,473
And I still pray to God
it's just a menopausal infatuation.

1232
01:15:21,392 --> 01:15:24,769
But it is an infatuation, Louise.

1233
01:15:26,355 --> 01:15:30,150
There's no sense in my saying
I won't see her again, because I will.

1234
01:15:34,238 --> 01:15:38,533
Do you want me to leave?
Check into a hotel?

1235
01:15:41,287 --> 01:15:42,954
Do you love her?

1236
01:15:46,626 --> 01:15:48,585
I don't know how I feel.

1237
01:15:50,963 --> 01:15:52,547
I'm grateful I can feel anything.

1238
01:15:57,303 --> 01:15:59,095
I know I'm obsessed with her.

1239
01:16:01,390 --> 01:16:03,183
Then say it.

1240
01:16:04,143 --> 01:16:07,896
Don't keep telling me that
you're obsessed, that you're infatuated.

1241
01:16:08,064 --> 01:16:10,315
Say that you're in love with her.

1242
01:16:12,860 --> 01:16:14,236
I'm in love with her.

1243
01:16:15,404 --> 01:16:17,197
Then get out!

1244
01:16:17,365 --> 01:16:20,992
Go anywhere you want. Go to a hotel,
go live with her, but don't come back.

1245
01:16:21,160 --> 01:16:22,827
Because after 25 years...

1246
01:16:22,995 --> 01:16:26,748
...of building a home and raising a family
and all the senseless pain...

1247
01:16:26,916 --> 01:16:30,669
...that we have inflicted on each other,
I'm damned if I'm gonna stand here...

1248
01:16:30,836 --> 01:16:33,505
...and have you tell me
you're in love with somebody else.

1249
01:16:34,090 --> 01:16:38,718
Because this isn't a convention weekend
with your secretary, is it?

1250
01:16:38,886 --> 01:16:43,181
Or some broad that you picked up
after three belts of booze.

1251
01:16:43,349 --> 01:16:46,101
This is your great winter romance,
isn't it?

1252
01:16:46,269 --> 01:16:50,188
Your last roar of passion before you settle
into your emeritus years.

1253
01:16:50,356 --> 01:16:52,065
Is that what's left for me?

1254
01:16:52,233 --> 01:16:56,278
Is that my share? She gets
the winter passion and I get the dotage.

1255
01:16:56,445 --> 01:16:57,696
What am I supposed to do?

1256
01:16:57,863 --> 01:17:01,574
Am I supposed to sit home knitting
and purling while you slink back...

1257
01:17:01,742 --> 01:17:03,868
...like some penitent drunk?

1258
01:17:04,328 --> 01:17:06,079
I'm your wife, damn it.

1259
01:17:06,247 --> 01:17:08,373
If you can't work up
a winter passion for me...

1260
01:17:08,541 --> 01:17:11,543
...the least I require
is respect and allegiance.

1261
01:17:14,171 --> 01:17:15,880
[SOBBING]

1262
01:17:24,056 --> 01:17:27,434
LOUISE:
I hurt, don't you understand that?

1263
01:17:29,562 --> 01:17:32,105
I hurt badly.

1264
01:17:32,732 --> 01:17:34,566
[SOBBING]

1265
01:17:40,740 --> 01:17:42,824
Oh, say something, for God's sake.

1266
01:17:52,585 --> 01:17:54,794
I've got nothing to say.

1267
01:18:05,598 --> 01:18:08,099
I won't give you up easily, Max.

1268
01:18:14,273 --> 01:18:17,108
I think perhaps it is better
if you move out.

1269
01:18:22,990 --> 01:18:25,200
Does she love you, Max?

1270
01:18:29,163 --> 01:18:32,832
I'm not sure she's capable
of any real feelings.

1271
01:18:33,000 --> 01:18:37,087
She's television generation.
She learned life from Bugs Bunny.

1272
01:18:37,254 --> 01:18:41,257
The only reality she knows
comes to her over the TV set.

1273
01:18:42,635 --> 01:18:45,428
She's very carefully devised
a number of scenarios...

1274
01:18:45,596 --> 01:18:49,349
...for all of us to play,
like the Movie of the Week.

1275
01:18:52,311 --> 01:18:54,646
My God, look at us, Louise.

1276
01:18:55,022 --> 01:18:58,441
Here we are going through
the obligatory middle of Act 2...

1277
01:18:58,609 --> 01:19:02,445
...scorned-wife-throws
peccant-husband-out scene.

1278
01:19:02,613 --> 01:19:05,824
But don't worry,
I'll come back to you in the end.

1279
01:19:05,991 --> 01:19:08,284
All of her plot outlines
have me leaving her...

1280
01:19:08,452 --> 01:19:11,204
...and coming back to you,
because the audience won't buy...

1281
01:19:11,372 --> 01:19:14,082
...a rejection
of the happy American family.

1282
01:19:16,919 --> 01:19:20,171
She does have one script
in which I kill myself.

1283
01:19:20,464 --> 01:19:25,218
An adapted for television version
of Anna Karenina...

1284
01:19:26,554 --> 01:19:29,055
...where she's Count Vronsky
and I'm Anna.

1285
01:19:29,223 --> 01:19:30,890
[LAUGHS]

1286
01:19:34,228 --> 01:19:36,438
You're in for some dreadful grief, Max.

1287
01:19:39,275 --> 01:19:40,817
I know.

1288
01:19:41,277 --> 01:19:44,112
NARRATOR: The Mao Tse-Tung Hour
went on the air March 14.

1289
01:19:44,280 --> 01:19:46,531
It received a 47 share.

1290
01:19:46,699 --> 01:19:50,618
The network promptly committed
to 15 shows with an option for 10 more.

1291
01:19:50,786 --> 01:19:53,037
There were the usual
contractual difficulties.

1292
01:19:53,205 --> 01:19:57,000
"Equal to 20 percent, 20, except that
such percentages shall be 30 percent, 30...

1293
01:19:57,168 --> 01:19:59,669
...for 90-minute or longer
television programs."

1294
01:19:59,879 --> 01:20:01,754
Have we settled that sublicensing thing?

1295
01:20:01,922 --> 01:20:05,175
- No.
- We want a clear definition here.

1296
01:20:06,302 --> 01:20:10,680
"Gross proceeds should consist
of all funds the sublicensee receives...

1297
01:20:10,848 --> 01:20:15,643
...not merely the net amount remitted after
payment to the sublicensee or distributor."

1298
01:20:15,811 --> 01:20:19,481
We're not sitting still for overhead charges
as a cost prior to distribution.

1299
01:20:19,648 --> 01:20:22,942
Don't fuck with my distribution costs.

1300
01:20:23,110 --> 01:20:24,944
I'm making a lousy 215 per segment.

1301
01:20:25,112 --> 01:20:27,530
I'm already deficiting $25,000 a week
with Metro!

1302
01:20:27,698 --> 01:20:29,949
I'm paying William Morris
10 percent off the top!

1303
01:20:30,117 --> 01:20:33,244
I'm giving this turkey $10,000
and another five to this fruitcake.

1304
01:20:33,412 --> 01:20:35,371
Don't start no shit
with me about a piece.

1305
01:20:35,539 --> 01:20:39,626
I'm paying Metro 20 percent for all foreign
and Canadian distribution after recoupment.

1306
01:20:39,793 --> 01:20:43,463
The Communist Party's not gonna see
a nickel until we go into syndication!

1307
01:20:43,631 --> 01:20:47,050
Come on, Laureen. The Party's in
for 7500 a week production expenses.

1308
01:20:47,218 --> 01:20:50,637
I'm not giving this pseudo-insurrectionary
sectarian a piece of my show.

1309
01:20:50,804 --> 01:20:54,849
I'm not giving him script approval. I'm not
cutting him in on my distribution charges.

1310
01:20:55,017 --> 01:20:56,851
GIFFORD:
You fucking fascist!

1311
01:20:57,019 --> 01:20:59,771
Did you see the film we made
of San Marino jail breakout...

1312
01:20:59,939 --> 01:21:03,441
...demonstrating the rising up of
the seminal prisoner-class infrastructure?

1313
01:21:03,609 --> 01:21:06,736
You can blow the seminal prisoner-class
infrastructure out your ass!

1314
01:21:06,904 --> 01:21:09,489
I'm not knocking down
my goddamn distribution charges.

1315
01:21:10,783 --> 01:21:15,245
Man, give her the fucking overhead clause.

1316
01:21:15,412 --> 01:21:17,997
How did I get here?
Who's gonna believe this?

1317
01:21:18,165 --> 01:21:20,625
I'm sitting here in a goddamn farmhouse
in Encino....

1318
01:21:20,793 --> 01:21:26,339
Let's get back to Page 22,
5, small "A", Subsidiary Rights.

1319
01:21:26,840 --> 01:21:27,882
Where are we now?

1320
01:21:28,050 --> 01:21:30,301
Page 22, middle of the page.
Subsidiary Rights.

1321
01:21:30,469 --> 01:21:34,097
"'Subsidiary rights' means
without limitation any and all rights...."

1322
01:21:34,348 --> 01:21:36,808
[ALL CHATTERING]

1323
01:21:45,317 --> 01:21:49,821
Over the past two days, you've all had
opportunity to meet Diana Christensen...

1324
01:21:49,989 --> 01:21:53,074
...our vice president
in charge of programming.

1325
01:21:53,242 --> 01:21:57,787
This afternoon, you all saw some of
the stuff she's set up for the new season.

1326
01:21:57,955 --> 01:22:00,248
[ALL CHEERING AND APPLAUDING]

1327
01:22:07,172 --> 01:22:10,967
You all know that she is the woman
behind the Howard Beale Show.

1328
01:22:11,135 --> 01:22:13,344
[ALL CHEERING AND APPLAUDING]

1329
01:22:19,768 --> 01:22:21,477
We all know she's beautiful.

1330
01:22:22,563 --> 01:22:24,772
We all know she's brainy.

1331
01:22:25,357 --> 01:22:30,987
I was thinking, before we start digging
into our Chateaubriands...

1332
01:22:32,197 --> 01:22:34,907
...let's show her how we feel about her.

1333
01:22:35,075 --> 01:22:37,368
[ALL CHEERING AND APPLAUDING]

1334
01:22:50,299 --> 01:22:52,884
We have the number-one show
in television!

1335
01:22:53,052 --> 01:22:55,053
[ALL CHEER]

1336
01:22:56,305 --> 01:22:58,056
At next year's affiliates' meeting...

1337
01:22:58,223 --> 01:23:00,975
...I'll be standing here telling you
we've got the top five.

1338
01:23:01,143 --> 01:23:03,394
[ALL CHEERING AND APPLAUDING]

1339
01:23:07,232 --> 01:23:10,068
Last year, we were
the number-four network...

1340
01:23:10,569 --> 01:23:12,570
...next year we're number one!

1341
01:23:13,322 --> 01:23:17,408
MAN:
We're number one! We're number one!

1342
01:23:17,576 --> 01:23:19,202
ALL [CHANTING]:
We're number one!

1343
01:23:19,370 --> 01:23:21,162
We're number one!

1344
01:23:21,330 --> 01:23:23,122
We're number one!

1345
01:23:23,290 --> 01:23:25,416
We're number one!

1346
01:23:28,420 --> 01:23:31,714
It is exactly 7:00 here in Los Angeles.

1347
01:23:31,924 --> 01:23:35,927
And right now, over a million homes
using television in this city...

1348
01:23:36,095 --> 01:23:40,598
...are turning their dials to Channel 3
and that's our channel!

1349
01:23:40,766 --> 01:23:42,934
[WHISPERS INDISTINCTLY]

1350
01:23:47,898 --> 01:23:49,524
ANNOUNCER:
Howard Beale!

1351
01:23:49,692 --> 01:23:51,776
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

1352
01:23:52,611 --> 01:23:54,487
Stop it, stop it!

1353
01:23:55,322 --> 01:23:56,447
Now you listen to me.

1354
01:23:56,615 --> 01:24:02,286
And listen carefully because this is your
goddamn life I'm talking about today.

1355
01:24:03,205 --> 01:24:06,499
In this country, when one company wants
to take over another company...

1356
01:24:06,667 --> 01:24:08,960
...they buy up a controlling share
of the stock...

1357
01:24:09,128 --> 01:24:11,796
...but first they have to file notice
with the government.

1358
01:24:11,964 --> 01:24:14,716
That's how CCA took over the company
that owns this network.

1359
01:24:14,883 --> 01:24:17,885
But now, somebody's buying up CCA.

1360
01:24:18,053 --> 01:24:21,597
Somebody called
the Western World Funding Corporation.

1361
01:24:21,765 --> 01:24:23,391
They filed the notice this morning.

1362
01:24:23,559 --> 01:24:28,187
Well, just who in the hell is
the Western World Funding Corporation?

1363
01:24:28,397 --> 01:24:31,733
It is a consortium of banks
and insurance companies...

1364
01:24:31,900 --> 01:24:35,361
...who are not buying CCA for themselves,
but as agents for somebody else.

1365
01:24:35,529 --> 01:24:37,739
Who is this somebody else?
They won't tell you.

1366
01:24:37,906 --> 01:24:40,199
They won't tell you,
they won't tell the Senate...

1367
01:24:40,367 --> 01:24:44,370
...they won't tell the SEC, the FTC,
they won't tell the Justice Department....

1368
01:24:44,538 --> 01:24:47,248
This is Mr. Hackett.
Do you have a New York call for me?

1369
01:24:47,416 --> 01:24:50,168
HOWARD: The hell it ain't!
-Do you wanna turn that down, please?

1370
01:24:50,335 --> 01:24:52,712
I will tell you
who they're buying CCA for.

1371
01:24:52,880 --> 01:24:54,172
[LOWERS VOLUME]

1372
01:24:54,339 --> 01:24:58,050
They're buying it for the Saudi Arabian
Investment Corporation.

1373
01:24:58,218 --> 01:25:00,219
They're buying it for the Arabs!

1374
01:25:00,512 --> 01:25:01,846
Clarence? Frank Hackett here.

1375
01:25:02,014 --> 01:25:05,308
How's everything back in New York?
How's the good lady?

1376
01:25:08,353 --> 01:25:12,356
All right, Clarence, take it easy.
I don't know what you're talking about.

1377
01:25:12,524 --> 01:25:18,362
When? Tonight's show?
Clarence, take it easy.

1378
01:25:19,531 --> 01:25:21,699
The Howard Beale Show
is just going on out here.

1379
01:25:21,867 --> 01:25:25,203
You guys get it three hours earlier
in New York. Clarence, take it easy.

1380
01:25:25,370 --> 01:25:28,372
How the hell could I see it?
It's just going on now!

1381
01:25:28,540 --> 01:25:32,210
HOWARD: And there's not a single law
in the books to stop them.

1382
01:25:33,545 --> 01:25:36,005
When did Mr. Jensen call?

1383
01:25:36,673 --> 01:25:42,887
We all know that the Arabs control
$16 billion in this country.

1384
01:25:43,055 --> 01:25:44,931
They own a chunk of 5th Avenue...

1385
01:25:45,098 --> 01:25:49,393
...twenty downtown pieces of Boston.
A part of the port of New Orleans.

1386
01:25:49,561 --> 01:25:52,021
An industrial park in Salt Lake City.

1387
01:25:52,189 --> 01:25:57,318
They own big hunks of the Atlanta Hilton,
the Arizona Land and Cattle Company...

1388
01:25:57,486 --> 01:25:59,237
...part of a bank in California...

1389
01:25:59,404 --> 01:26:01,364
...the Bank of the Commonwealth
in Detroit.

1390
01:26:01,532 --> 01:26:05,910
They control Aramco, so that puts
them into Exxon, Texaco and Mobil Oil.

1391
01:26:06,078 --> 01:26:10,289
They're all over! New Jersey,
Louisville, St. Louis, Missouri...

1392
01:26:10,457 --> 01:26:12,375
...and that's only what we know about.

1393
01:26:12,543 --> 01:26:15,127
There's a hell of a lot more
we don't know about.

1394
01:26:15,295 --> 01:26:17,755
Because all of those Arab petrol dollars...

1395
01:26:17,923 --> 01:26:20,258
...are washed through
Switzerland and Canada...

1396
01:26:20,425 --> 01:26:22,343
...and the biggest banks in this country.

1397
01:26:22,511 --> 01:26:26,222
For example, what we don't know
about is this CCA deal...

1398
01:26:26,890 --> 01:26:29,392
...and all the other CCA deals.

1399
01:26:29,852 --> 01:26:33,688
Right now the Arabs have screwed us
out of enough American dollars...

1400
01:26:33,856 --> 01:26:37,233
...to come right back and, with our
own money, buy General Motors...

1401
01:26:37,401 --> 01:26:41,612
...IBM, ITT, AT&T, Dupont, U.S. Steel...

1402
01:26:41,780 --> 01:26:44,073
...and 20 other American companies.

1403
01:26:44,241 --> 01:26:49,537
Hell, they already own half of England.
So listen to me.

1404
01:26:49,705 --> 01:26:53,958
Listen to me, goddamn it.
The Arabs are simply buying us.

1405
01:26:54,793 --> 01:26:57,628
There's only one thing
that can stop them. You!

1406
01:26:58,589 --> 01:27:00,339
You!

1407
01:27:00,591 --> 01:27:03,384
So I want you to get up now.

1408
01:27:03,594 --> 01:27:06,304
I want you to get up out of your chairs.

1409
01:27:06,471 --> 01:27:09,265
I want you to get up right now
and go to the phone.

1410
01:27:09,433 --> 01:27:13,311
I want you to get up from your chairs,
go to the phone, get in your cars...

1411
01:27:13,478 --> 01:27:15,980
...drive into the Western Union
offices in town.

1412
01:27:16,148 --> 01:27:19,483
I want you to send a telegram
to the White House.

1413
01:27:19,651 --> 01:27:22,028
- Oh, my God.
- By midnight tonight...

1414
01:27:22,195 --> 01:27:24,989
...I want a million telegrams
in the White House.

1415
01:27:25,157 --> 01:27:29,118
I want them wading knee-deep
in telegrams at the White House.

1416
01:27:29,369 --> 01:27:34,415
I want you to get up right now and write
a telegram to President Ford saying:

1417
01:27:34,583 --> 01:27:38,461
"I'm as mad as hell
and I'm not gonna take this anymore.

1418
01:27:38,629 --> 01:27:41,672
I don't want the banks
selling my country to the Arabs.

1419
01:27:41,840 --> 01:27:45,009
I want the CCA deal stopped now.

1420
01:27:45,177 --> 01:27:48,429
I want the CCA deal stopped now.
Come on.

1421
01:27:48,597 --> 01:27:51,849
AUDIENCE:
I want the CCA deal stopped now!

1422
01:27:52,017 --> 01:27:55,061
I want the CCA deal stopped now!

1423
01:27:55,228 --> 01:27:58,314
I want the CCA deal stopped now!

1424
01:27:58,482 --> 01:28:00,524
I want the CCA deal stopped now!

1425
01:28:00,692 --> 01:28:02,985
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

1426
01:28:11,536 --> 01:28:13,120
[TONE DRONING]

1427
01:28:14,873 --> 01:28:17,708
- Look, could we have the room?
MAN: Sure.

1428
01:28:26,134 --> 01:28:30,221
Well, I'd like to see a typescript
and run through a couple more times.

1429
01:28:30,806 --> 01:28:33,891
But as for this whole CCA deal
with the Saudis...

1430
01:28:34,059 --> 01:28:36,727
...you'd know a lot more
about that, Frank, than I would.

1431
01:28:36,895 --> 01:28:38,646
Is it true?

1432
01:28:42,234 --> 01:28:46,070
The CCA has 2 billion in loans
with the Saudis...

1433
01:28:46,279 --> 01:28:49,240
...and they hold every pledge we've got.

1434
01:28:50,492 --> 01:28:53,244
We need that Saudi money bad.

1435
01:28:55,414 --> 01:28:58,332
Disaster. The show is a disaster.

1436
01:28:58,500 --> 01:28:59,583
[SIGHS]

1437
01:28:59,751 --> 01:29:02,920
Unmitigated disaster. The death knell.

1438
01:29:03,088 --> 01:29:04,255
[SIGHS]

1439
01:29:04,423 --> 01:29:08,259
I'm ruined. I'm dead. Finished.

1440
01:29:08,927 --> 01:29:12,847
Maybe we're overstating
Beale's clout with the public.

1441
01:29:14,016 --> 01:29:16,600
An hour ago, Clarence McElheny
called me from New York.

1442
01:29:16,768 --> 01:29:19,979
It was 10:00 in the east and our people
in the White House report...

1443
01:29:20,147 --> 01:29:22,982
...they were already knee-deep in telegrams.

1444
01:29:23,150 --> 01:29:28,029
By tomorrow morning,
they'll be suffocating in telegrams.

1445
01:29:28,196 --> 01:29:30,823
- Can the government stop the deal?
- They can hold it up.

1446
01:29:30,991 --> 01:29:34,410
The SEC could hold this deal up
for 20 years, if they wanted to.

1447
01:29:34,661 --> 01:29:36,037
I'm finished.

1448
01:29:36,204 --> 01:29:39,707
Any second that phone's gonna ring
and Clarence McElheny is gonna tell me...

1449
01:29:39,875 --> 01:29:42,710
...Mr. Jensen wants me in his office
tomorrow morning...

1450
01:29:42,878 --> 01:29:46,338
...so he can personally chop my head off.

1451
01:29:47,007 --> 01:29:49,383
Four hours ago,
I was the sun god at CCA.

1452
01:29:49,551 --> 01:29:53,637
Mr. Jensen's hand-picked golden boy,
the heir apparent.

1453
01:29:53,805 --> 01:29:58,392
Now, ha, ha,
I'm a man without a corporation.

1454
01:29:59,478 --> 01:30:01,645
DIANA:
Let's get back to Howard Beale.

1455
01:30:02,981 --> 01:30:06,150
You're not seriously gonna pull Beale
off the air?

1456
01:30:08,278 --> 01:30:10,279
[FRANK SIGHS]

1457
01:30:10,447 --> 01:30:14,450
Mr. Jensen's unhappy with Howard Beale
and wants him discontinued.

1458
01:30:14,618 --> 01:30:16,994
But he may be unhappy,
but he isn't stupid enough...

1459
01:30:17,162 --> 01:30:20,039
...to withdraw the number-one show
on television out of pique.

1460
01:30:20,207 --> 01:30:23,084
Two billion dollars isn't pique!
That's the wrath of God!

1461
01:30:23,251 --> 01:30:25,586
And the wrath of God
wants Howard Beale fired!

1462
01:30:25,754 --> 01:30:28,255
Every other network will grab him
the minute he walks.

1463
01:30:28,423 --> 01:30:31,133
He'll be back on the air for ABC
and we'll lose 20 points--

1464
01:30:31,301 --> 01:30:33,844
I'm gonna impale the son of a bitch
with a sharp stick!

1465
01:30:34,012 --> 01:30:36,680
DIANA: Forty million loss in revenues.
- I'll take out a contract.

1466
01:30:36,848 --> 01:30:40,142
- Let's not discount federal action....
- I'll hire professional killers.

1467
01:30:40,310 --> 01:30:45,481
No, I'll do it myself.
I'll strangle him with a sash cord!

1468
01:30:45,816 --> 01:30:48,984
--and a breach of the consent decree.
I don't think Jensen's gonna fire anybody.

1469
01:30:49,152 --> 01:30:51,237
[PHONE RINGING]

1470
01:30:54,783 --> 01:30:56,200
Hackett.

1471
01:30:58,411 --> 01:31:01,872
Yes, Clarence.
I've already booked my flight.

1472
01:31:03,583 --> 01:31:05,918
Uh, well, can you give me
a little more time than that?

1473
01:31:06,086 --> 01:31:08,796
I've got the red-eye flight,
I won't be back in New York...

1474
01:31:08,964 --> 01:31:11,132
...till 6 tomorrow morning.

1475
01:31:13,093 --> 01:31:15,136
That'll be just fine.

1476
01:31:15,387 --> 01:31:17,054
I'll see you then.

1477
01:31:25,689 --> 01:31:28,983
Mr. Jensen wants to meet
Howard Beale personally.

1478
01:31:29,526 --> 01:31:33,279
He wants Mr. Beale in his office
at 10:00 tomorrow morning.

1479
01:31:39,786 --> 01:31:42,496
The final revelation is at hand.

1480
01:31:42,664 --> 01:31:46,750
I have seen the shattering fulgurations
of ultimate clarity.

1481
01:31:46,918 --> 01:31:51,755
The light is impending.
I bear witness to the light!

1482
01:32:12,569 --> 01:32:14,153
JENSEN:
Good morning, Mr. Beale.

1483
01:32:14,321 --> 01:32:17,031
- They tell me you're a madman.
- Only desultorily.

1484
01:32:17,199 --> 01:32:19,533
- How are you now?
- I'm as mad as a hatter.

1485
01:32:19,701 --> 01:32:21,368
Who isn't?

1486
01:32:21,953 --> 01:32:24,121
I'm going to take you
into our conference room.

1487
01:32:24,289 --> 01:32:27,625
Seems more seemly a setting
for what I have to say to you.

1488
01:32:28,960 --> 01:32:31,378
I started as a salesman, Mr. Beale.

1489
01:32:31,546 --> 01:32:34,423
I sold sewing machines
and automobile parts...

1490
01:32:34,591 --> 01:32:37,509
...hairbrushes and electronic equipment.

1491
01:32:37,677 --> 01:32:40,012
They say I can sell anything.

1492
01:32:40,847 --> 01:32:44,099
I'd like to try to sell something to you.

1493
01:32:47,687 --> 01:32:51,315
Valhalla, Mr. Beale. Please, sit down.

1494
01:33:20,804 --> 01:33:25,599
You have meddled with the primal forces
of nature, Mr. Beale.

1495
01:33:25,767 --> 01:33:30,104
And I won't have it! Is that clear?

1496
01:33:30,397 --> 01:33:32,856
You think you've merely stopped
a business deal.

1497
01:33:33,024 --> 01:33:34,566
That is not the case.

1498
01:33:34,734 --> 01:33:37,653
The Arabs have taken billions of dollars
out of this country...

1499
01:33:37,821 --> 01:33:39,697
...and now they must put it back!

1500
01:33:39,864 --> 01:33:45,035
It is ebb and flow, tidal gravity,
it is ecological balance.

1501
01:33:46,621 --> 01:33:48,372
You are an old man...

1502
01:33:48,540 --> 01:33:52,376
...who thinks in terms
of nations and peoples.

1503
01:33:52,544 --> 01:33:55,921
There are no nations, there are no peoples.
There are no Russians.

1504
01:33:56,089 --> 01:33:58,549
There are no Arabs.
There are no Third Worlds.

1505
01:33:58,717 --> 01:33:59,883
There is no West!

1506
01:34:00,051 --> 01:34:05,014
There is only one holistic system
of systems.

1507
01:34:05,181 --> 01:34:07,391
One vast and immane...

1508
01:34:07,559 --> 01:34:10,394
...interwoven, interacting, multi-variate...

1509
01:34:10,562 --> 01:34:13,731
...multinational dominion of dollars.

1510
01:34:13,898 --> 01:34:17,026
Petrol dollars, electro-dollars,
multi-dollars.

1511
01:34:17,193 --> 01:34:22,948
Reichsmarks, rins, rubles,
pounds and shekels.

1512
01:34:24,284 --> 01:34:28,746
It is the international system of currency
which determines...

1513
01:34:28,913 --> 01:34:32,291
...the totality of life on this planet.

1514
01:34:33,251 --> 01:34:37,755
That is the natural order of things today.

1515
01:34:38,882 --> 01:34:42,634
That is the atomic...

1516
01:34:42,802 --> 01:34:44,928
...and subatomic...

1517
01:34:45,096 --> 01:34:50,434
...and galactic structure
of things today.

1518
01:34:51,186 --> 01:34:53,270
And you have meddled...

1519
01:34:53,438 --> 01:34:57,983
...with the primal forces of nature!

1520
01:34:58,276 --> 01:35:03,781
And you will atone.

1521
01:35:04,407 --> 01:35:06,784
Am I getting it through to you, Mr. Beale?

1522
01:35:10,246 --> 01:35:14,792
You get up on your little 21-inch screen...

1523
01:35:15,502 --> 01:35:20,381
...and howl about America
and democracy.

1524
01:35:20,965 --> 01:35:25,302
There is no America.
There is no democracy.

1525
01:35:25,470 --> 01:35:30,974
There is only IBM and ITT and AT&T...

1526
01:35:31,142 --> 01:35:36,730
...and Dupont, Dow,
Union Carbide, and Exxon.

1527
01:35:36,898 --> 01:35:40,484
Those are the nations of the world today.

1528
01:35:40,860 --> 01:35:44,988
What do you think the Russians talk about
in their councils of state? Karl Marx?

1529
01:35:45,156 --> 01:35:47,491
They get out their
linear programming charts...

1530
01:35:47,659 --> 01:35:50,160
...statistical decision theories,
minimax solutions...

1531
01:35:50,328 --> 01:35:53,789
...and compute price-cost probabilities
of transactions and investments...

1532
01:35:53,957 --> 01:35:54,998
...just like we do.

1533
01:35:55,500 --> 01:35:59,753
We no longer live in a world of nations
and ideologies, Mr. Beale.

1534
01:35:59,921 --> 01:36:04,591
The world is a college of corporations...

1535
01:36:05,260 --> 01:36:12,141
...inexorably determined
by the immutable bylaws of business.

1536
01:36:14,227 --> 01:36:17,187
The world is a business, Mr. Beale.

1537
01:36:19,107 --> 01:36:23,068
It has been since man
crawled out of the slime.

1538
01:36:25,864 --> 01:36:30,784
And our children will live, Mr. Beale...

1539
01:36:32,162 --> 01:36:33,745
...to see that...

1540
01:36:36,040 --> 01:36:38,792
...perfect world...

1541
01:36:39,794 --> 01:36:43,005
...in which there's no war or famine...

1542
01:36:43,173 --> 01:36:46,508
...oppression or brutality.

1543
01:36:47,552 --> 01:36:51,513
One vast and ecumenical
holding company...

1544
01:36:51,681 --> 01:36:55,976
...for whom all men will work
to serve a common profit...

1545
01:36:56,144 --> 01:37:00,397
...in which all men will hold
a share of stock...

1546
01:37:01,649 --> 01:37:04,568
...all necessities provided...

1547
01:37:05,278 --> 01:37:09,114
...all anxieties tranquillized...

1548
01:37:10,074 --> 01:37:13,994
...all boredom amused.

1549
01:37:19,959 --> 01:37:24,546
And I have chosen you, Mr. Beale...

1550
01:37:24,714 --> 01:37:27,216
...to preach this evangel.

1551
01:37:27,884 --> 01:37:29,510
Why me?

1552
01:37:30,762 --> 01:37:33,597
Because you're on television, dummy.

1553
01:37:34,474 --> 01:37:39,937
Sixty million people watch you every night
of the week, Monday through Friday.

1554
01:37:40,813 --> 01:37:43,106
I have seen the face of God.

1555
01:37:45,652 --> 01:37:48,237
You just might be right, Mr. Beale.

1556
01:37:49,781 --> 01:37:52,115
NARRATOR: That evening,
Howard Beale went on the air...

1557
01:37:52,283 --> 01:37:54,952
...to preach the corporate cosmology
of Arthur Jensen.

1558
01:37:55,119 --> 01:37:57,996
Last night I got up here
and asked you people...

1559
01:37:58,164 --> 01:38:02,459
...to stand up and fight for your heritage,
and you did, and it was beautiful.

1560
01:38:02,627 --> 01:38:05,629
Six million telegrams were received
at the White House.

1561
01:38:05,797 --> 01:38:08,966
The Arab takeover of CCA
has been stopped.

1562
01:38:09,133 --> 01:38:14,805
The people spoke, the people won.
It was a radiant eruption of democracy.

1563
01:38:14,973 --> 01:38:19,017
But I think that was it, fellas.

1564
01:38:19,185 --> 01:38:21,895
That sort of thing is not likely
to happen again.

1565
01:38:22,105 --> 01:38:25,065
Because at the bottom
of all our terrified souls...

1566
01:38:25,233 --> 01:38:28,277
...we know that democracy
is a dying giant...

1567
01:38:28,444 --> 01:38:33,240
...a sick, sick, dying, decaying,
political concept writhing in its final pain.

1568
01:38:33,408 --> 01:38:36,994
I don't mean that the United States
is finished as a world power.

1569
01:38:37,161 --> 01:38:39,329
The States is the richest
and most powerful...

1570
01:38:39,497 --> 01:38:42,457
...the most advanced country,
light years ahead of any country.

1571
01:38:42,625 --> 01:38:45,335
I don't mean the communists
are gonna take over the world.

1572
01:38:45,503 --> 01:38:48,839
The communists are deader than we are.
What is finished...

1573
01:38:50,466 --> 01:38:53,927
...is the idea that this great country
is dedicated to the freedom...

1574
01:38:54,095 --> 01:38:57,806
...and flourishing of every individual in it.

1575
01:38:58,891 --> 01:39:01,852
It's the individual that's finished.

1576
01:39:02,270 --> 01:39:06,189
It's the single, solitary, human being
that's finished.

1577
01:39:07,066 --> 01:39:11,111
It's every single one of you out there
that's finished.

1578
01:39:11,654 --> 01:39:13,864
Because this is no longer...

1579
01:39:14,032 --> 01:39:17,743
...a nation of independent individuals.

1580
01:39:18,036 --> 01:39:20,829
It's a nation of some 200-odd million...

1581
01:39:20,997 --> 01:39:23,540
...transistorized, deodorized...

1582
01:39:23,708 --> 01:39:29,212
...whiter than white steel-belted bodies,
totally unnecessary as human beings...

1583
01:39:29,380 --> 01:39:32,758
...and as replaceable as piston rods.

1584
01:39:43,394 --> 01:39:46,605
Well, the time has come to say...

1585
01:39:46,773 --> 01:39:49,941
...is "dehumanization" such a bad word?

1586
01:39:50,318 --> 01:39:53,403
Whether it's good or bad,
that's what is so.

1587
01:39:53,571 --> 01:39:58,742
The whole world is becoming humanoid,
creatures that look human but aren't.

1588
01:39:59,202 --> 01:40:00,577
The whole world, not just us.

1589
01:40:00,745 --> 01:40:04,915
We're just the most advanced country,
so we're getting there first.

1590
01:40:05,583 --> 01:40:10,545
The whole world's people are becoming
mass-produced, programmed...

1591
01:40:10,713 --> 01:40:12,464
...numbered insensate things.

1592
01:40:12,882 --> 01:40:14,925
NARRATOR:
It was a perfectly admissible argument...

1593
01:40:15,093 --> 01:40:17,678
...that Howard Beale advanced
in the days that followed.

1594
01:40:17,845 --> 01:40:20,722
It was, however,
also a very depressing one.

1595
01:40:20,890 --> 01:40:24,226
Nobody particularly cared to hear
his life was utterly valueless.

1596
01:40:24,394 --> 01:40:26,228
By the end of the first week in June...

1597
01:40:26,396 --> 01:40:29,147
...the Howard Beale Show
dropped one point in the ratings...

1598
01:40:29,315 --> 01:40:33,944
...and its trend of shares dipped under 48
for the first time since last November.

1599
01:40:34,112 --> 01:40:38,115
You're his goddamn agent. I'm counting
on you to talk some sense into the lunatic.

1600
01:40:38,282 --> 01:40:41,785
Nobody wants to hear about
dying democracy and dehumanization.

1601
01:40:42,412 --> 01:40:43,495
I'm sorry I'm late.

1602
01:40:43,663 --> 01:40:45,872
We're starting to get rumbles
from the agencies.

1603
01:40:46,040 --> 01:40:48,834
Another couple of weeks
and the sponsors will be bailing out!

1604
01:40:49,001 --> 01:40:52,129
This is a breach of contract.
This isn't the Howard Beale we signed.

1605
01:40:52,296 --> 01:40:56,591
Get him off that corporate universe kick,
or so help me, I'll pull it off the air!

1606
01:40:56,759 --> 01:40:59,886
I told him, Lou! I've been telling him
every day for a week!

1607
01:41:00,054 --> 01:41:03,140
I'm sick of telling him. Now you tell him!

1608
01:41:07,812 --> 01:41:09,312
[SIGHS]

1609
01:41:11,023 --> 01:41:12,399
Jesus Christ.

1610
01:41:15,903 --> 01:41:18,238
You could help me out
with Howard if you wanted to.

1611
01:41:18,406 --> 01:41:20,657
He listens to you. You're his best friend.

1612
01:41:20,825 --> 01:41:23,285
I'm tired of all this hysteria
about Howard Beale.

1613
01:41:23,453 --> 01:41:26,121
Every time you come
from seeing somebody in your family...

1614
01:41:26,289 --> 01:41:28,623
...you come back in one of these
middle-aged moods.

1615
01:41:28,791 --> 01:41:31,835
I'm tired of finding you on the telephone
every time I turn around.

1616
01:41:32,003 --> 01:41:34,838
I'm tired of being an accessory
in your life.

1617
01:41:35,298 --> 01:41:37,841
And I'm tired of pretending to write
this dumb book...

1618
01:41:38,009 --> 01:41:41,178
...about my maverick days
in the great early years of television.

1619
01:41:41,345 --> 01:41:45,015
Every goddamned executive fired
from a network in the last 20 years...

1620
01:41:45,183 --> 01:41:49,186
...has written this dumb book
about the great early years of television.

1621
01:41:49,353 --> 01:41:52,647
And nobody wants
a dumb, damn, goddamn book...

1622
01:41:52,815 --> 01:41:55,025
...about the early days of television.

1623
01:41:55,193 --> 01:41:58,236
Terrific, Max! Maybe you can start
a whole new career as an actor.

1624
01:41:58,404 --> 01:42:00,113
MAX:
It's the truth.

1625
01:42:00,865 --> 01:42:05,619
After living with you for six months,
I'm turning into one of your scripts.

1626
01:42:06,412 --> 01:42:08,872
Well, this is not a script, Diana.

1627
01:42:09,207 --> 01:42:12,834
There's some real, actual life
going on here.

1628
01:42:13,628 --> 01:42:17,214
I went to visit my wife today
because she's in a state of depression...

1629
01:42:17,423 --> 01:42:21,051
...so depressed that my daughter flew
all the way from Seattle to be with her.

1630
01:42:21,219 --> 01:42:23,220
And I feel lousy about that.

1631
01:42:23,387 --> 01:42:27,516
I feel lousy about the pain
that I've caused my wife and my kids.

1632
01:42:27,683 --> 01:42:29,601
I feel guilty and conscience-stricken...

1633
01:42:29,769 --> 01:42:32,395
...and all of those things
that you think sentimental...

1634
01:42:32,563 --> 01:42:36,525
...but which my generation
calls simple, human decency.

1635
01:42:40,530 --> 01:42:42,572
And I miss my home...

1636
01:42:43,282 --> 01:42:46,117
...because I'm beginning
to get scared shitless.

1637
01:42:46,285 --> 01:42:49,746
Because all of a sudden it's closer
to the end than it is to the beginning.

1638
01:42:49,914 --> 01:42:52,874
And death is suddenly
a perceptible thing to me...

1639
01:42:53,042 --> 01:42:55,544
...with definable features.

1640
01:42:59,590 --> 01:43:03,969
You're dealing with a man
that has primal doubts, Diana...

1641
01:43:04,303 --> 01:43:06,763
...and you've got to cope with it.

1642
01:43:07,348 --> 01:43:11,434
I'm not some guy discussing male
menopause on the Barbara Walters Show.

1643
01:43:12,103 --> 01:43:15,438
I'm the man that you presumably love.

1644
01:43:16,524 --> 01:43:19,442
I'm part of your life.

1645
01:43:19,610 --> 01:43:23,280
I live here. I'm real.

1646
01:43:24,448 --> 01:43:27,325
You can't switch to another station.

1647
01:43:34,792 --> 01:43:37,627
What exactly is it you want me to do?

1648
01:43:41,632 --> 01:43:44,676
I just want you to love me.

1649
01:43:45,928 --> 01:43:49,389
I just want you to love me,
primal doubts and all.

1650
01:43:51,726 --> 01:43:54,144
You understand that, don't you?

1651
01:43:59,150 --> 01:44:01,443
I don't know how to do that.

1652
01:44:02,695 --> 01:44:04,487
[PHONE RINGING]

1653
01:44:13,164 --> 01:44:15,790
I'll be with you in a minute, Max.

1654
01:44:20,922 --> 01:44:22,422
NARRATOR:
By the first week in July...

1655
01:44:22,590 --> 01:44:24,716
...the Howard Beale Show
was down 11 points.

1656
01:44:24,884 --> 01:44:26,718
Hysteria swept through the network.

1657
01:44:26,886 --> 01:44:28,553
He's a plague. He's smallpox.

1658
01:44:28,721 --> 01:44:31,222
He's typhoid.
I don't wanna follow his goddamn show.

1659
01:44:31,390 --> 01:44:32,724
I want out of that 8:00 spot.

1660
01:44:32,892 --> 01:44:35,602
I've got enough troubles
without Howard Beale as a lead-in!

1661
01:44:35,770 --> 01:44:37,854
Scheduled me against
Tony Orlando and Dawn.

1662
01:44:38,022 --> 01:44:41,274
NBC's got Little House on the Prairie.
ABC's got The Bionic Woman.

1663
01:44:41,442 --> 01:44:44,027
Do something! You gotta do something
about Howard Beale!

1664
01:44:44,195 --> 01:44:46,363
Get him off the air! Get him off!

1665
01:44:46,530 --> 01:44:48,156
Do something! Do anything!

1666
01:44:48,324 --> 01:44:50,325
We're trying to find a replacement
for him!

1667
01:44:50,493 --> 01:44:52,535
I'm going to look
at audition footage now!

1668
01:44:52,787 --> 01:44:56,247
MAN [ON SCREEN]:
And how when the sicks heal...

1669
01:44:56,415 --> 01:44:59,376
...man, I tell you I saw it!

1670
01:45:00,211 --> 01:45:05,298
It was heavy, baby.
I saw the earth quake.

1671
01:45:05,466 --> 01:45:09,219
And I saw the moon became like blood.

1672
01:45:09,387 --> 01:45:13,264
And every mountain and island
was moved from its place.

1673
01:45:13,432 --> 01:45:15,684
No, no, no. Damn it.

1674
01:45:15,851 --> 01:45:17,852
If we wanted hellfire
we'd get Billy Graham!

1675
01:45:18,020 --> 01:45:21,398
Don't want faith healers, evangelists
or Oberammergau passion players!

1676
01:45:21,565 --> 01:45:24,609
What about that messiah
that ABC was supposed to have signed up...

1677
01:45:24,777 --> 01:45:27,445
- ...as our competition for next year?
MAN: That's him.

1678
01:45:27,613 --> 01:45:31,908
- The bottomless pit is here.
DIANA: That's him?

1679
01:45:32,076 --> 01:45:33,952
His ass ending.

1680
01:45:34,120 --> 01:45:36,162
Jesus. Turn him off!

1681
01:45:37,289 --> 01:45:41,084
I've got three more,
but you've already seen the best ones.

1682
01:45:41,252 --> 01:45:44,087
I've got a guru from Spokane
and two more hellfires...

1683
01:45:44,255 --> 01:45:46,047
...who see visions of the Virgin Mary.

1684
01:45:46,215 --> 01:45:50,010
We're not gonna find a replacement for
Howard Beale. Let's stop kidding ourselves.

1685
01:45:50,177 --> 01:45:53,013
Fully fledged messiahs
don't come in bunches.

1686
01:45:53,180 --> 01:45:56,349
We either go with Howard Beale
or we go without him.

1687
01:45:56,517 --> 01:45:59,394
My reports say
we'll do better without him.

1688
01:45:59,562 --> 01:46:02,439
It would be disaster to let this situation
go on another week.

1689
01:46:02,606 --> 01:46:05,233
By then, he'll be down 16 points...

1690
01:46:05,401 --> 01:46:08,778
...and the trend irreversible,
if it isn't already.

1691
01:46:09,989 --> 01:46:13,074
I think we should fire Howard.

1692
01:46:15,870 --> 01:46:21,624
Arthur Jensen has taken a strong personal
interest in the Howard Beale Show.

1693
01:46:23,627 --> 01:46:27,088
I'm having dinner with him tonight.
Let me have another crack at Jensen...

1694
01:46:27,256 --> 01:46:29,674
...and then let's meet in my office
at 10:00 tonight.

1695
01:46:29,842 --> 01:46:32,635
Diana, give me copies
of all your audience research reports.

1696
01:46:32,803 --> 01:46:36,931
I may need them for Jensen.
Is 10:00 convenient for everyone?

1697
01:47:07,797 --> 01:47:08,797
[DIANA CHUCKLES]

1698
01:47:08,964 --> 01:47:13,218
I think the time has come
to re-evaluate our relationship, Max.

1699
01:47:13,844 --> 01:47:15,512
So I see.

1700
01:47:17,098 --> 01:47:20,475
I don't like the way this script of ours
is turning out.

1701
01:47:20,643 --> 01:47:23,436
It's turning into a seedy little drama.

1702
01:47:23,604 --> 01:47:27,941
Middle-aged man leaves wife and family
for young heartless woman, goes to pot.

1703
01:47:28,109 --> 01:47:31,861
The Blue Angel with Marlene Dietrich
and Emil Jannings. I don't like it.

1704
01:47:32,029 --> 01:47:34,114
- So you're gonna cancel the show.
- Right.

1705
01:47:34,281 --> 01:47:36,199
Here, let me do that.

1706
01:47:37,785 --> 01:47:42,914
The simple fact is, Max,
that you're a family man.

1707
01:47:43,082 --> 01:47:46,835
You like a home and kids. That's beautiful.
I'm incapable of any such commitment.

1708
01:47:47,002 --> 01:47:49,921
All you'll get from me is
a couple months of intermittent sex...

1709
01:47:50,089 --> 01:47:53,466
...and recriminate and ugly little scenes
like the one we had last night.

1710
01:47:53,634 --> 01:47:57,220
I'm sorry for all those things
I said to you last night.

1711
01:47:57,388 --> 01:48:01,724
You're not the worst fuck I've ever had.
Believe me, I've had worse.

1712
01:48:02,226 --> 01:48:05,603
You don't puff or snorkle...

1713
01:48:05,771 --> 01:48:07,480
...and make death-like rattles.

1714
01:48:07,648 --> 01:48:10,441
As a matter of fact,
you're rather serene in the sack.

1715
01:48:11,777 --> 01:48:13,653
Why is it that a woman always thinks...

1716
01:48:13,821 --> 01:48:19,033
...that the most savage thing she can say
to a man is to impugn his cocksmanship?

1717
01:48:20,244 --> 01:48:23,580
Well, I'm sorry I impugned
your cocksmanship.

1718
01:48:24,248 --> 01:48:28,042
I gave up comparing genitals
back in the schoolyard.

1719
01:48:37,678 --> 01:48:40,430
You're being docile as hell about this.

1720
01:48:41,473 --> 01:48:44,976
Oh, hell, Diana,
I knew it was over with us weeks ago.

1721
01:48:45,311 --> 01:48:47,979
Will you go back to your wife?

1722
01:48:49,982 --> 01:48:52,775
I'll give it a try,
but I don't think she'll jump at it.

1723
01:48:52,943 --> 01:48:55,195
But don't worry about me. I'll manage.

1724
01:48:55,362 --> 01:48:59,699
I always have, I always will.
I'm more concerned about you.

1725
01:49:00,534 --> 01:49:02,285
You're not the boozer type.

1726
01:49:02,453 --> 01:49:05,997
So I figure a year, maybe two,
before you crack up.

1727
01:49:06,165 --> 01:49:08,833
Or jump out of your 14th floor
office window.

1728
01:49:09,001 --> 01:49:12,212
Stop selling, Max. I don't need you.

1729
01:49:23,599 --> 01:49:27,477
I don't want your pain. I don't want
your menopausal decay and death!

1730
01:49:27,645 --> 01:49:28,728
I don't need you, Max.

1731
01:49:28,896 --> 01:49:32,649
- Now get out of here!
- You need me! You need me badly.

1732
01:49:32,816 --> 01:49:35,610
Because I'm your last contact
with human reality.

1733
01:49:35,778 --> 01:49:37,779
I love you.

1734
01:49:37,947 --> 01:49:41,950
And that painful, decaying love
is the only thing between you...

1735
01:49:42,117 --> 01:49:45,036
...and the shrieking nothingness
you live the rest of the day.

1736
01:49:45,204 --> 01:49:46,829
Then don't leave me.

1737
01:49:49,959 --> 01:49:52,168
It's too late, Diana.

1738
01:49:53,295 --> 01:49:56,172
There's nothing left in you
that I can live with.

1739
01:49:58,884 --> 01:50:01,427
You're one of Howard's humanoids...

1740
01:50:01,595 --> 01:50:04,264
...and if I stay with you,
I'll be destroyed.

1741
01:50:04,932 --> 01:50:07,517
Like Howard Beale was destroyed.

1742
01:50:08,018 --> 01:50:10,645
Like Laureen Hobbs was destroyed.

1743
01:50:11,188 --> 01:50:15,024
Like everything that you
and the institution of television touch...

1744
01:50:15,192 --> 01:50:17,235
...is destroyed.

1745
01:50:23,033 --> 01:50:25,034
You're television incarnate, Diana.

1746
01:50:26,453 --> 01:50:31,833
Indifferent to suffering, insensitive to joy.

1747
01:50:33,127 --> 01:50:37,171
All of life is reduced
to the common rubble of banality.

1748
01:50:40,884 --> 01:50:43,803
War, murder, death...

1749
01:50:44,555 --> 01:50:47,724
...all the same to you
as bottles of beer.

1750
01:50:48,267 --> 01:50:52,937
And the daily business of life
is a corrupt comedy.

1751
01:50:54,106 --> 01:50:57,483
You even shatter the sensations
of time and space...

1752
01:50:57,651 --> 01:51:02,405
...into split seconds and instant replays.

1753
01:51:06,160 --> 01:51:07,869
You're madness, Diana.

1754
01:51:09,705 --> 01:51:12,040
Virulent madness.

1755
01:51:13,751 --> 01:51:16,878
And everything you touch dies with you.

1756
01:51:21,717 --> 01:51:23,509
But not me.

1757
01:51:24,470 --> 01:51:30,141
Not as long
as I can feel pleasure and pain...

1758
01:51:33,937 --> 01:51:35,646
...and love.

1759
01:51:47,076 --> 01:51:48,159
And it's a happy ending.

1760
01:51:50,454 --> 01:51:54,123
Wayward husband comes to his senses...

1761
01:51:54,750 --> 01:51:56,334
...returns to his wife...

1762
01:51:56,543 --> 01:51:59,545
...with whom he's established
a long and sustaining love.

1763
01:52:00,756 --> 01:52:04,801
Heartless young woman left alone
in her arctic desolation.

1764
01:52:07,846 --> 01:52:10,139
Music up with a swell.

1765
01:52:13,060 --> 01:52:14,852
Final commercial.

1766
01:52:17,481 --> 01:52:21,067
And here are a few scenes
from next week's show.

1767
01:52:25,948 --> 01:52:27,490
[DOOR CLOSES]

1768
01:52:32,996 --> 01:52:34,872
How did it go?

1769
01:52:51,515 --> 01:52:56,686
FRANK: Mr. Jensen was unhappy at the idea
of taking Howard Beale off the air.

1770
01:52:57,938 --> 01:53:01,858
Mr. Jensen thinks Howard Beale
is bringing a very important message...

1771
01:53:02,025 --> 01:53:04,444
...to the American people.

1772
01:53:05,779 --> 01:53:09,365
So he wants Howard Beale on the air
and he wants him kept on.

1773
01:53:11,618 --> 01:53:14,620
Mr. Jensen feels we're too catastrophic
in our thinking.

1774
01:53:14,788 --> 01:53:18,958
I argued that television was a volatile
industry in which success and failure...

1775
01:53:19,126 --> 01:53:21,711
...were determined week by week.

1776
01:53:22,379 --> 01:53:25,882
Mr. Jensen said he did not like
volatile industries and suggested...

1777
01:53:26,049 --> 01:53:29,552
...with a certain sinister silkiness...

1778
01:53:30,429 --> 01:53:34,056
...that volatility in business
usually reflected bad management.

1779
01:53:35,058 --> 01:53:38,311
He didn't care if Howard Beale
was the number-one show or the 50th.

1780
01:53:38,479 --> 01:53:40,938
He didn't really care
if the Beale Show lost money.

1781
01:53:42,149 --> 01:53:46,611
He wants Howard Beale on the air
and he wants him kept on.

1782
01:53:47,321 --> 01:53:51,991
I would describe his position on this
as inflexible.

1783
01:53:52,743 --> 01:53:55,119
Where does that put us, Diana?

1784
01:53:55,996 --> 01:53:59,916
That puts us in the shithouse,
that's where that puts us.

1785
01:54:02,544 --> 01:54:05,379
- Do you want me to go through this?
FRANK: Yes.

1786
01:54:06,465 --> 01:54:10,760
The Beale Show Q score's down to 33.

1787
01:54:11,428 --> 01:54:14,889
Most of this loss occurred in the child
and teen and 18-34 categories...

1788
01:54:15,057 --> 01:54:18,309
...which were our key core markets.

1789
01:54:18,519 --> 01:54:21,646
And as the AR department's carefully
considered judgment and mine...

1790
01:54:21,813 --> 01:54:25,191
...that if we get rid of Beale,
we should maintain a respectable share...

1791
01:54:25,359 --> 01:54:28,236
...in the high 20s, possibly 30,
with a comparable Q level.

1792
01:54:28,403 --> 01:54:30,947
The other segments of the show,
Sibyl the Soothsayer...

1793
01:54:31,114 --> 01:54:35,284
...Jim Webbing, the Vox Populi,
have all developed their own audiences.

1794
01:54:35,452 --> 01:54:37,620
Our AR reports show
that it is Howard Beale...

1795
01:54:37,788 --> 01:54:40,623
...that is the destructive force here.

1796
01:54:41,208 --> 01:54:46,003
Minimally, we're talking about
a 10-point differential in shares.

1797
01:54:46,964 --> 01:54:49,966
I think Joe ought
to spell it out for us. Joe?

1798
01:54:50,467 --> 01:54:53,594
A 28 share is 80,000-dollar minutes.

1799
01:54:53,762 --> 01:54:56,389
I think we can sell complete positions
on the whole.

1800
01:54:56,557 --> 01:54:59,183
We're just getting
into the pre-Christmas gift sellers...

1801
01:54:59,351 --> 01:55:02,895
...and I'll tell you the agencies are coming
back to me with $4 CPM's.

1802
01:55:03,063 --> 01:55:07,316
If that's any indication, we're talking 40-,
45 million-dollar loss in annual revenues.

1803
01:55:07,484 --> 01:55:09,485
Wanna hear the flak from the affiliates?

1804
01:55:09,653 --> 01:55:11,153
FRANK:
We know all about it, Herb.

1805
01:55:11,321 --> 01:55:15,116
And you would describe Mr. Jensen's
position on Beale as inflexible?

1806
01:55:15,617 --> 01:55:18,119
Intractable and adamantine.

1807
01:55:19,997 --> 01:55:23,165
So, what do we do
about this Beale son of a bitch?

1808
01:55:25,335 --> 01:55:27,420
I suppose we'll have to kill him.

1809
01:55:30,340 --> 01:55:33,426
I don't suppose you have any ideas
on that, Diana?

1810
01:55:40,142 --> 01:55:43,185
Well, what would you fellows say
to an assassination?

1811
01:55:44,688 --> 01:55:48,691
I think I can get the Mao Tse-Tung people
to kill Beale for us...

1812
01:55:48,859 --> 01:55:50,026
...as one of their shows.

1813
01:55:51,236 --> 01:55:55,698
In fact, it'll make a hell of a kickoff show
for the season.

1814
01:55:55,866 --> 01:55:59,368
We're facing heavy opposition on the
other networks for Wednesday nights...

1815
01:55:59,536 --> 01:56:02,955
...and The Mao Tse-Tung Hour
could use a sensational opener.

1816
01:56:04,416 --> 01:56:08,210
It could be done
right on camera in the studio.

1817
01:56:09,880 --> 01:56:12,048
We ought to get
a fantastic look-in audience...

1818
01:56:12,215 --> 01:56:16,177
...for the assassination
of Howard Beale as our opening show.

1819
01:56:16,345 --> 01:56:21,057
MAN: Well, if Beale dies, what would
our continuing obligation...

1820
01:56:21,224 --> 01:56:23,267
...to the Beale corporation be?

1821
01:56:23,560 --> 01:56:26,395
I know our contract with Beale
contains a buy-out clause...

1822
01:56:26,563 --> 01:56:28,689
...triggered by his death or incapacity.

1823
01:56:28,857 --> 01:56:32,151
There must be a formula
for the computation of the purchase price.

1824
01:56:32,319 --> 01:56:36,280
Offhand, I think it was based
on a multiple 1975 earnings...

1825
01:56:36,490 --> 01:56:38,574
...with the base period in 1975.

1826
01:56:38,992 --> 01:56:43,037
I think it was 50 percent of salary
plus 25 percent of the first year's profit...

1827
01:56:43,205 --> 01:56:46,499
...multiplied by the unexpired portion
of the contract.

1828
01:56:46,667 --> 01:56:49,627
I don't think the show has
any substantial syndication value...

1829
01:56:49,795 --> 01:56:50,961
...would you say, Diana?

1830
01:56:51,129 --> 01:56:52,838
Syndication profits are minimal.

1831
01:56:54,174 --> 01:56:56,842
We're talking about a capital crime here.

1832
01:56:57,969 --> 01:57:00,513
The network can't be implicated.

1833
01:57:00,681 --> 01:57:03,015
[AUDIENCE CHATTERING]

1834
01:57:11,024 --> 01:57:15,236
I hope you don't have any hidden
tape machines in this office, Frank.

1835
01:57:17,364 --> 01:57:20,241
FRANK: Well, the issue is,
shall we kill Howard Beale or not?

1836
01:57:20,409 --> 01:57:22,868
I'd like to hear
some more opinions on that.

1837
01:57:23,036 --> 01:57:26,455
I don't see we have any option, Frank.
Let's kill the son of a bitch.

1838
01:57:26,707 --> 01:57:30,084
Ladies and gentlemen, let's hear it.
How do you feel?

1839
01:57:30,252 --> 01:57:34,630
ALL: We're mad as hell
and we're not going to take this anymore!

1840
01:57:34,798 --> 01:57:36,882
ANNOUNCER: Ladies and gentlemen,
the Network News Hour...

1841
01:57:37,050 --> 01:57:39,301
...with Sibyl the Soothsayer.

1842
01:57:39,469 --> 01:57:41,971
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

1843
01:57:42,139 --> 01:57:45,808
Jim Webbing and his It's-the-Emes
Truth Department.

1844
01:57:48,562 --> 01:57:52,440
Ms. Mata Hari and her
Skeletons in the Closet.

1845
01:57:55,152 --> 01:57:57,486
And tonight,
another segment of Vox Populi.

1846
01:58:02,033 --> 01:58:06,662
And starring the Mad Prophet
of the Airways, Howard Beale!

1847
01:58:26,141 --> 01:58:30,519
ANCHOR: The Network News anchorman
on the UBS Network News show...

1848
01:58:30,687 --> 01:58:34,565
...known to millions as the Mad Prophet
of the Airways...

1849
01:58:34,733 --> 01:58:38,569
...was shot to death tonight
in a fusillade of automatic-rifle fire...

1850
01:58:38,737 --> 01:58:41,530
...just as he began
this evening's broadcast.

1851
01:58:41,698 --> 01:58:43,783
ANNOUNCER: We never compromise,
so why should you?

1852
01:58:43,950 --> 01:58:46,327
Canada Dry mixers, why compromise?

1853
01:58:46,495 --> 01:58:49,538
ANCHOR: --identified themselves as
the group responsible for the killing.

1854
01:58:49,706 --> 01:58:53,209
Ahmed Kahn, a massive man of well
over 6 feet, carrying an automatic weapon.

1855
01:58:53,376 --> 01:58:55,044
BOY 1:
--supposed to be good for you.

1856
01:58:55,212 --> 01:58:58,756
- Did you try it?
BOY 2: I'm not gonna try it, you try it.

1857
01:58:58,924 --> 01:59:02,009
- I'm not gonna try it.
- Let's get Mikey.

1858
01:59:02,219 --> 01:59:05,054
BOY 1: Yeah. He won't eat it.
He hates everything.

1859
01:59:05,222 --> 01:59:06,722
ANCHOR:
The extraordinary incident...

1860
01:59:06,890 --> 01:59:09,141
...occurred in full view
of his millions of viewers.

1861
01:59:09,309 --> 01:59:11,560
The assassins were members
of a terrorist group...

1862
01:59:11,728 --> 01:59:15,815
...called the Ecumenical Liberation Army,
two of whom were apprehended.

1863
01:59:15,982 --> 01:59:19,401
The leader of the group, known
as the Great Ahmed Kahn, escaped.

1864
01:59:19,820 --> 01:59:22,112
NARRATOR:
This was the story of Howard Beale...

1865
01:59:22,280 --> 01:59:24,824
...the first known instance
of a man who was killed...

1866
01:59:24,991 --> 01:59:26,617
...because he had lousy ratings.

1867
01:59:26,785 --> 01:59:29,036
[OVERLAPPING TV CHATTER]

1868
02:01:16,019 --> 02:01:18,020
[ENGLISH - US - SDH]

